✅2.6 Why is Runnable preferred over extending Thread?

Problems solved by Runnable

1. Supports Single Inheritance
Java supports only one class inheritance.

With Thread:
class MyThread extends Thread

You cannot write:
class MyThread extends Thread, Employee

With Runnable:

class MyTask extends Employee implements Runnable
✔️ Perfectly valid.

2. Separation of Responsibility

Runnable follows the Single Responsibility Principle.
Runnable   → What to execute
Thread     → How to execute

Example:

Downloading File
        │
        ▼
    Runnable

Worker Thread
        │
        ▼
    Thread
3. Better Reusability

🔴 The same Runnable task can be executed by:

Multiple Thread objects
ExecutorService
Thread Pools
Scheduled Executors

without changing the task implementation.

4. Modern Java Uses Executors

Modern applications rarely create threads manually.

Instead:

Business Logic
        │
        ▼
    Runnable
        │
        ▼
ExecutorService / Thread Pool / Thread

This makes the design:

Flexible
Reusable
Maintainable
Scalable